Local changes to reel-kit 1.2.0 (upstream: Justyn Berkovits, MIT). Re-apply after the next upgrade; each is small.

1. pipeline/cut.py: SPEED. A piece of the take can be played faster (atempo + setpts) for a drawn-out word. Kept from 1.0.
   E.SPEED = {piece index: factor}; segs carry "sp"; pieces() returns a 5-tuple (out_start, out_end, src, frame, sp).
   Audio joins inside a sped word get a 6 ms fade instead of a dip. (Upstream 1.2.0 still lacks this, applied clean.)
2. setup/setup.py and setup/setup.sh: Python 3.12 minimum (build.py uses f-string syntax that only parses on 3.12+).
   Upstream still says 3.10+.
Dropped because 1.2.0 now has them: common.clip_start never negative, fxsandbox links the project's style/, setup --check skips the render test.

